      {
        "id": 387005,
        "name": "Master of Monsters",
        "summary": "The Genesis/Mega Drive port of \"Master of Monsters\".\n\nMaster of Monsters is a turn-based strategy game developed by SystemSoft for the MSX and NEC PC8801. It was ported to a variety of consoles and PCs including the PC Engine CD, NEC PC9801, and Sega Genesis/Mega Drive. While it never had the same success as its SystemSoft stablemate Daisenryaku, the game garnered a loyal following. Its success in the North American market on the Sega Genesis proved sufficient for a sequel on the Sega Saturn, and an anime art-style enhanced Sony PlayStation version.\n\nA European release for Mega Drive was planned by Ubisoft but it did not materialise.",
